# Object repository conventions

Read `Commons/object_repository.py` and the target app's existing YAML. Keep
locators under `ObjectRepository/<APP>/`; reuse repository keys in app methods
and testcase steps instead of embedding selectors in testcase workbooks.

## YAML structure

`page` prefixes entries under `elements`. Filter group names under `groups` are
already complete keys: they are not prefixed with `page`.

```yaml
page: DataSets
elements:
  RowsPerPage-Dd: //*[@class='dropdown']/button
groups:
  DataSets/Repository:
    checkboxes:
      CEDCD: //*[@value='CEDCD']
      GEO: //*[@value='GEO']
      dbGaP: //*[@value='dbGaP']
```

- Define each checkbox explicitly under `checkboxes`, one value and locator per
  line. Do not introduce `checkbox_template` or compact `values` lists.
- The group key is the first `select_filter(group, value)` argument; the checkbox
  map key is the second. Preserve each app's established tokens and capitalization.
- Define each element/group in one canonical YAML location. The loader reads all
  YAML recursively; duplicate keys can silently overwrite earlier definitions.
  If compatibility requires an existing duplicate, keep definitions aligned and
  document it; do not add new duplicates or remove existing ones as unrelated work.
- Use `facet`, `dropdown`/`dropdowns`, and `search` only when the observed control
  requires them. Follow the loaded `FilterGroup` contract; do not invent fields.

## Selector quality and validation

- Inspect the actual target environment when adding or repairing locators.
  Prefer stable IDs, test IDs, roles, labels, or meaningful link destinations.
- Avoid generated CSS class suffixes, exact whole-class matches, and long
  absolute/positional XPaths when a stable scoped selector is available.
- Scope repeated labels to the correct panel/table. Check visibility and match
  count; do not use `.first` to mask an accidentally ambiguous selector.
- Resolve dropdown options by their value/text rather than their list position.
- Respect lazy rendering and collapsed facets; use the shared filter-opening
  methods rather than duplicating accordion or scrolling logic.
- Parse changed YAML and resolve affected keys through `ObjectRepository`.
  Exercise changed selectors on the UI when available. Report if live validation
  could not be completed; a syntactically valid XPath is not a verified locator.
